## Splice point 4b: .../kernel_ingestor_engine/IngestorPacks.cpp
## Add this row to the s_packs table. Both this edit AND the IngestorPacks.hpp
## declaration edit (ingestor_packs.hpp.txt) are required -- see that fragment's
## header for why.
##
## The struct is (label, registerSymbols, ownsModuleCache, resetModuleCache).
## ownsModuleCache and resetModuleCache must agree -- TestIngestorPacksModuleCacheOwnership
## asserts `ownsModuleCache == (resetModuleCache != nullptr)` for every pack. That test
## passes for BOTH shapes, so it cannot tell you which one you needed.
##
## The discriminator is whether your dispatch handler ROUTES THROUGH
## buildIngestorKernelCode, not which dialect your kernels use. That function takes a
## `const compilation::KpackKernelLoader&` (IngestorKernelCode.hpp:237), so any handler
## calling it holds a loader and owns a module cache:
##   * handler routes through buildIngestorKernelCode -> true, &reset<Name>ModuleCache
##     (declare it in the .hpp too, and define it OUTSIDE the pack's anonymous namespace)
##   * handler does not route                         -> false, nullptr
## hipkernel:Pointwise is the worked example of the first: it ships
## `true, &resetPointwiseModuleCache` (IngestorPacks.cpp:16) even though its kernels are
## embedded_source. hipkernel:ConvFwd does not route and ships `false, nullptr` (:19).
##
## This fragment can see the dialect but not whether you routed, so it emits the
## dialect-based answer as a starting point. hipdnn-kernel-integration's RUNBOOK step 3
## mandates routing through buildIngestorKernelCode, so an engine that follows it needs
## `true, &reset...` even on the else-branch below. Correct the emitted row to match your
## handler; a routed pack left at `false, nullptr` never drops its module cache.
## Check the IngestorPack struct before splicing: this row must match it field for field.
{% if config.is_packaged -%}
## Packaged dialect: this engine owns a kpack module cache, so it must drop it. Define
## reset{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}ModuleCache outside the pack's anonymous namespace
## and declare it in IngestorPacks.hpp beside the register function.
        {"{{ config.engine.name }}", &{{ config.register_symbols_fn }}, true, &reset{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}ModuleCache},
{% else -%}
## direct_load/embedded_source: no archive is held, so there is nothing to drop.
        {"{{ config.engine.name }}", &{{ config.register_symbols_fn }}, false, nullptr},
{% endif -%}
